              evaluation: `This is clearly Tier A. Peer-reviewed Nature Neuroscience publication; specific methodology with controls; quantified findings; appropriate discussion of limits. Establishes that music can produce dopamine release at peak emotion moments through measurable neural mechanism. Does not establish: specific music or genres are more "dopaminergic" in general; the dopamine release is what makes music meaningful (correlation isn't full explanation); music therapy applications follow directly (clinical applications require separate research). Limits worth noting: small sample (8); self-selected music; PET imaging has temporal resolution limits; "peak emotion" operationalized as "chills" which is one specific phenomenon. How to cite: when someone says "music releases dopamine," this study is one of the foundational sources; the citation should note both the finding and its appropriate scope.`,
