              type: `Quality popular science / clinical narrative`,
              context: `Late neurologist Oliver Sacks's exploration of music's effects on the brain through case studies of patients with various neurological conditions. Includes Alzheimer's patients who recognize music when they recognize little else; stroke patients who can sing what they can't say; epilepsy patients whose seizures are triggered by specific music; people who become musical savants after brain injury; many others. Substantial scholarly engagement throughout; accessible to general readers.`,
